Subject: [PATCH v3 1/6] claude/skills/process-email: Take the message to
 answer as an argument
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: ktpzmqruykkypmyrnnkzlstxlspzwnuw

A pass picked its own message with a notmuch query, so whatever ran it
could not say which message that pass was for, and so could not check
afterwards that this message was answered. Choosing the next message
needs no judgement, and leaving it to the model means a driver and the
model could disagree on it.

The skill now requires a notmuch id and answers only that message. The
skill no longer loops over the inbox; draining it is left to a caller
that runs one pass per message. A named message that is no longer in
the inbox ends the pass without writing, because someone has already
answered or archived it.
